  "query_preview": ".. (Monday through Next Thursday)\n\nUpper-level height rises and an amplifying western ridge will \nbuild back into the Great Lakes early next week, bringing a \nswift return to seasonably warm, dry, and pleasant summer \nconditions for Monday and Tuesday. Highs will rebound back into \nthe mid-80s under mostly sunny skies. \n\nThe next opportunity for showers and thunderstorms arrives mid-\nweek as a robust northern-stream shortwave drives a cold front \ntoward the Upper Midwest. However, model guidance displays \nconsiderable spread regarding frontal penetration into central \nIllinois as the primary upper-level dynamics rapidly displace \neastward into Canada. Will maintain lower-end rain chances (20%)\nfor Wednesday into Thursday to account for lingering timing and\nboundary position uncertainties.",
